  "body": "Add active template mutation records\n\nAdd an `activeTemplateAttributeFilter` member to `MutationObserverInit`, and `activeTemplateStatus` and `activeTemplateAttributes` attributes to `MutationRecord`. This lets observers identify the mutations that the HTML parser makes on behalf of a `template` element with a `for` attribute, including records with no added or removed nodes that mark the start and end of an update.\n\nThe insert, remove, and queue a tree mutation record algorithms gain optional activeTemplate and activeTemplateStatus parameters for HTML to pass.\n\n`childList` no longer defaults to false, so that it can be implied when `activeTemplateAttributeFilter` is given.\n\nTests: https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/64641.\n\nHelps with https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/13008.\n\n---\n\nThe HTML side is whatwg/html#13181. The two PRs need to land together.\n\nI drafted this PR, the HTML PR, and the tests with an AI coding agent (Gemini in Antigravity), based on the proposed design in whatwg/html#13008 and the [explainer](https://github.com/WICG/declarative-partial-updates/blob/main/template-mutation-observer-explainer.md). I made the judgement calls: explicit optional parameters on insert, remove, and queue a tree mutation record; implying `childList` when the filter is given and throwing a `TypeError` when `childList` is explicitly false; and caching the attributes object per observer and per active template, so all records for one `<template for>` share an object that can be used as a `WeakMap` key.\n\n- [ ] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * …\n   * …\n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/64641\n- [ ] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * Chromium: …\n   * Gecko: …\n   * WebKit: …\n- [ ] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed: …\n- [x] The top of this comment includes a [clear commit message](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/COMMITTING.md) to use.\n\n(See [WHATWG Working Mode: Changes](https://whatwg.org/working-mode#changes) for more details.)\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/dom/1518.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 17, 2026, 4:30 PM UTC (b6e28f4)\">Preview</a> | <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/dom/1518/3c53f93...b6e28f4.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 17, 2026, 4:30 PM UTC (b6e28f4)\">Diff</a>",
